WEBVTT

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.776
Regeneration phase completed.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.108
Deactivate the genotron.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.043
Shut down the bio-matrix.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:25.187
B'Elanna...

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.989
B'Elanna Torres.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:30.359
Wake up.

00:02:20.571 --> 00:02:24.439
Captain's Log, Stardate 48784.2.

00:02:24.475 --> 00:02:27.171
We have completed our survey
of the Avery system

00:02:27.211 --> 00:02:28.542
and are returning to retrieve

00:02:28.579 --> 00:02:30.979
Lieutenants Paris,
Torres and Durst.

00:02:31.082 --> 00:02:33.312
By now, they should have
concluded their inspection

00:02:33.351 --> 00:02:36.343
of the magnesite formations
on the third planet.

00:02:36.387 --> 00:02:40.483
Here we are, Mr. Tuvok.

00:02:40.525 --> 00:02:44.985
One bowl of authentic
Vulcan plomeek soup.

00:02:45.096 --> 00:02:47.087
As I have told you, Mr. Neelix,

00:02:47.131 --> 00:02:48.826
this is
an unnecessary indulgence.

00:02:48.866 --> 00:02:50.424
I am quite content to eat

00:02:50.468 --> 00:02:51.958
whatever the rest of the crew
is eating.

00:02:52.003 --> 00:02:52.970
Nonsense!

00:02:53.004 --> 00:02:54.369
Everyone aboard this ship

00:02:54.405 --> 00:02:57.806
deserves a little taste of home
every now and then.

00:02:57.842 --> 00:02:59.366
Very well, then.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:00.809
Thank you.

00:03:00.845 --> 00:03:02.745
Oh, don't thank me.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.179
I'm having a marvelous time

00:03:04.215 --> 00:03:05.512
experimenting
with the native dishes

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:06.778
of the entire crew.

00:03:06.817 --> 00:03:10.378
So far, I've learned to make
corn salad for Mr. Chakotay

00:03:10.421 --> 00:03:12.719
and peanut butter
and jelly sandwiches

00:03:12.757 --> 00:03:14.190
for Mr. Paris.

00:03:14.225 --> 00:03:16.352
He calls it "comfort food."

00:03:16.394 --> 00:03:17.759
Isn't that charming?

00:03:19.263 --> 00:03:21.197
What are you waiting for?
It's no good cold.

00:03:27.004 --> 00:03:28.972
Well?

00:03:30.474 --> 00:03:32.533
It is rather... piquant.

00:03:32.577 --> 00:03:34.442
It is zesty, isn't it?

00:03:34.478 --> 00:03:37.777
I tried following the recipe
in the computer's data bank,

00:03:37.815 --> 00:03:39.407
but it seemed so bland.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:42.283
So I took the liberty
of spicing it up a bit.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.255
Call it plomeek soup
à la Neelix.

00:03:45.289 --> 00:03:47.519
I must point out
that if you take the liberty

00:03:47.558 --> 00:03:49.992
of changing
a time-honored recipe,

00:03:50.027 --> 00:03:52.723
you are hardly presenting
a taste of home.

00:03:52.763 --> 00:03:55.960
Senior officers,
please report to the Bridge.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.160
But your soup.

00:03:57.201 --> 00:03:58.668
Please...

00:03:58.703 --> 00:04:00.227
enjoy it.

00:04:11.449 --> 00:04:13.849
Oh!

00:04:13.884 --> 00:04:15.875
Ooh, there's no place like home.

00:04:17.288 --> 00:04:18.778
The away team hasn't arrived

00:04:18.823 --> 00:04:20.484
at the prearranged coordinates,
Captain,

00:04:20.524 --> 00:04:22.685
and they've failed
to respond to our hails.

00:04:22.727 --> 00:04:25.059
Have you tried locking on
to their com signals?

00:04:25.096 --> 00:04:26.961
We scanned the entire surface.
No sign of them.

00:04:27.031 --> 00:04:28.089
They must still be underground.

00:04:28.132 --> 00:04:29.429
But I can't locate them
there, either.

00:04:29.467 --> 00:04:32.368
Then, as we suspected,
the dense magnesite formations

00:04:32.403 --> 00:04:35.600
in the planet's crust
are blocking our sensors.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.073
Take a look at this.

00:04:37.108 --> 00:04:38.973
This is the cave system
nearest the beam-in coordinates

00:04:39.043 --> 00:04:40.943
as it appeared in our
initial geological scan

00:04:40.978 --> 00:04:42.775
and this is
the same system now.

00:04:42.813 --> 00:04:44.110
This tunnel here

00:04:44.148 --> 00:04:46.412
has shifted to the west
by almost 75 degrees.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:49.146
Are you saying walls
of solid rock have changed shape

00:04:49.186 --> 00:04:51.313
in the two days since
the away team was deployed?

00:04:51.355 --> 00:04:53.346
Apparently so, Captain,
but our initial scans

00:04:53.391 --> 00:04:55.222
didn't indicate
tectonic activity

00:04:55.259 --> 00:04:56.988
of anywhere near that magnitude.

00:04:57.061 --> 00:04:59.256
In any case, it's possible
that Torres and the others

00:04:59.296 --> 00:05:01.924
haven't returned to the beam-out
site because they were trapped

00:05:01.999 --> 00:05:03.830
by these geological shifts.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:06.428
I'd like to lead a team
down to investigate, Captain.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.132
And what is to prevent us from
losing you as well, Commander?

00:05:09.173 --> 00:05:10.299
Bread crumbs.

00:05:10.341 --> 00:05:11.365
Ensign?

00:05:11.409 --> 00:05:12.899
Oh, I'm sorry, Captain.

00:05:12.943 --> 00:05:16.276
What I mean to say is
I think I can modify

00:05:16.313 --> 00:05:18.474
some subspace transponders
which could be deployed

00:05:18.516 --> 00:05:20.040
along the Commander's path,
kind of like...

00:05:20.084 --> 00:05:21.949
Bread crumbs.
Got it.

00:05:22.019 --> 00:05:23.486
If they're placed
at regular intervals,

00:05:23.521 --> 00:05:25.318
I believe they'll maintain
a signal link with the ship

00:05:25.356 --> 00:05:27.551
and they could serve
as a transporter relay

00:05:27.591 --> 00:05:29.650
in case we need to stage
an emergency beam-out.

00:05:31.829 --> 00:05:33.091
Very well, Commander.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:35.223
Take a team with you,
but I want a transporter lock

00:05:35.266 --> 00:05:36.631
on you at all times.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:37.634
Aye, Captain.

00:05:37.668 --> 00:05:39.636
Tuvok, Kim, you're with me.

00:05:51.248 --> 00:05:53.910
I apologize
for the restraints,

00:05:53.951 --> 00:05:56.749
but your presence here
is very important to us.

00:05:56.787 --> 00:05:58.880
Do you understand?

00:05:58.923 --> 00:06:02.222
Who... are... you?

00:06:02.259 --> 00:06:08.095
I am Sulan, Chief Surgeon
of the Vidiian Sodality.

00:06:08.132 --> 00:06:14.503
I demand... to know...

00:06:14.538 --> 00:06:17.632
what is happening here.

00:06:24.014 --> 00:06:27.950
You've surgically altered
my face!

00:06:28.052 --> 00:06:31.044
I look like a Klingon!

00:06:31.088 --> 00:06:34.455
I've performed no surgery,
as you understand the term.

00:06:34.492 --> 00:06:37.757
There are several questions
I need to ask you

00:06:37.795 --> 00:06:39.422
before we proceed.

00:06:39.463 --> 00:06:42.091
You can't possibly believe

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:44.966
I'm going to cooperate
with you.

00:06:45.002 --> 00:06:46.526
Perhaps I was in error

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:49.733
to leave your consciousness
and memory intact.

00:06:49.774 --> 00:06:52.834
Durst...

00:06:52.877 --> 00:06:55.141
Paris...

00:06:55.179 --> 00:06:58.307
What have you done with them?!

00:06:58.349 --> 00:07:00.943
What is your exact age,
Klingon?

00:07:00.985 --> 00:07:05.888
If you want me
to answer your question,

00:07:05.923 --> 00:07:09.825
you will have to answer
one of mine first.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.521
Very well.

00:07:11.562 --> 00:07:18.126
What... exactly...
have you done to me?

00:07:18.169 --> 00:07:20.637
I have reconstituted
your genome.

00:07:20.671 --> 00:07:22.935
You are now purely Klingon.

00:07:23.007 --> 00:07:24.942
That's not possible!

00:07:25.075 --> 00:07:27.566
I assure you it is.

00:07:27.611 --> 00:07:31.809
I have developed a procedure
to stimulate cell division.

00:07:31.848 --> 00:07:35.511
A kind of... enhanced mitosis.

00:07:35.552 --> 00:07:38.919
Your Klingon genetic material
was extracted.

00:07:38.956 --> 00:07:42.414
It was then converted
from matter to energy

00:07:42.459 --> 00:07:43.756
by our genotron.

00:07:43.794 --> 00:07:45.557
Finally...

00:07:45.595 --> 00:07:47.620
you were rematerialized

00:07:47.664 --> 00:07:50.565
as the purified
Klingon specimen

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:52.192
that you are now.

00:07:52.235 --> 00:07:54.795
Why? Why...

00:07:54.838 --> 00:07:56.305
have you done this?!

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.070
For generations,
my people have been searching

00:07:59.109 --> 00:08:02.169
the Quadrant
for a species immune

00:08:02.212 --> 00:08:05.670
to our disease, in the hope
that it would lead us to a cure.

00:08:05.716 --> 00:08:11.621
And you think Klingons
are immune to this phage?

00:08:11.655 --> 00:08:12.747
I believe your genetic structure

00:08:12.789 --> 00:08:16.316
has phage-resistant
nucleotide sequences, yes.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:21.525
But I needed a pure specimen
to be certain.

00:08:21.565 --> 00:08:24.295
My people do not know it yet,

00:08:24.334 --> 00:08:27.132
but you are their greatest hope.

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.866
I... will... never

00:08:29.906 --> 00:08:31.498
help you!

00:08:31.541 --> 00:08:33.941
You are very strong.

00:08:33.977 --> 00:08:38.607
I can only hope that you will be
truly resistant to the phage.

00:08:38.648 --> 00:08:42.778
And how will you know that?

00:08:42.819 --> 00:08:46.152
I have infected you.

00:09:15.318 --> 00:09:17.479
They're the ones
with the guns, remember?

00:09:32.736 --> 00:09:34.533
We've got to find a way
out of this place.

00:09:34.571 --> 00:09:37.301
Agreed, but I don't want
to do anything

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.205
until we find out what
they've done with B'Elanna.

00:09:43.814 --> 00:09:47.580
In the meantime, we have to keep
track of the guards' movements...

00:09:47.617 --> 00:09:49.084
how long are their shifts

00:09:49.119 --> 00:09:51.280
when do they eat,
when do they sleep.

00:09:54.658 --> 00:09:57.422
There don't seem
to be many of them.

00:09:57.461 --> 00:09:59.452
I guess they figure
we're all so exhausted,

00:09:59.496 --> 00:10:01.361
we don't have any fight left.

00:10:01.398 --> 00:10:03.263
We'll find an opening, Pete,

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:06.235
and when the time is right,
we'll make our move.

00:10:08.939 --> 00:10:10.338
Something funny, friend?

00:10:10.373 --> 00:10:11.806
You.

00:10:11.842 --> 00:10:12.968
Really?

00:10:13.043 --> 00:10:14.169
How's that?

00:10:14.211 --> 00:10:16.270
Nobody ever escapes
from this place.

00:10:16.313 --> 00:10:17.780
Those Vidiian leeches

00:10:17.814 --> 00:10:20.874
can yank the beating heart
out of you... in a heartbeat.

00:10:20.917 --> 00:10:23.215
Heart out of you
in a heartbeat.

00:10:23.253 --> 00:10:24.914
Now, that's funny.

00:10:24.955 --> 00:10:26.388
Hilarious.

00:10:26.423 --> 00:10:28.084
Seems like you know this place
pretty well.

00:10:28.125 --> 00:10:30.491
I should.
I've been here six years.

00:10:30.527 --> 00:10:33.360
Then tell me something...

00:10:33.396 --> 00:10:34.363
I thought those Vidiians

00:10:34.397 --> 00:10:36.991
were in the business
of harvesting organs.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.465
How come we're all
still in one piece?

00:10:38.502 --> 00:10:40.470
The disease makes them weak.

00:10:40.504 --> 00:10:42.438
They need somebody
to dig their tunnels.

00:10:42.472 --> 00:10:44.269
That's us.

00:10:44.307 --> 00:10:46.241
Best way to keep alive
around here

00:10:46.276 --> 00:10:48.335
is to stay strong.

00:10:49.379 --> 00:10:50.368
Thanks for the advice.

00:10:50.413 --> 00:10:51.641
But don't worry.

00:10:51.681 --> 00:10:53.842
They're always in need
of replacement body parts.

00:10:53.884 --> 00:10:56.114
They'll get around
to gutting you eventually.

00:10:56.153 --> 00:10:59.316
There were 23 of us
from my ship.

00:10:59.356 --> 00:11:01.620
I'm the only one left.

00:11:01.658 --> 00:11:03.888
Listen, when they grabbed us,

00:11:03.927 --> 00:11:07.363
there was a woman with us...
B'Elanna Torres.

00:11:07.397 --> 00:11:08.762
Any idea what might've
happened to her?

00:11:08.798 --> 00:11:10.231
If she's not here,

00:11:10.267 --> 00:11:12.428
she's been taken
to organ processing.

00:11:45.235 --> 00:11:47.897
I've deployed
the transponders, Commander.

00:11:47.938 --> 00:11:50.668
The relay signal
is coming through clearly.

00:11:50.707 --> 00:11:52.038
Good work.

00:11:58.815 --> 00:12:00.407
Any sign of them?

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.816
According
to my tricorder readings,

00:12:02.852 --> 00:12:04.752
they definitely
came this way.

00:12:04.788 --> 00:12:08.019
The question is: Where
did they go from here?

00:12:13.163 --> 00:12:15.961
Delightful spot to get lost.

00:12:16.066 --> 00:12:18.864
Commander, Ensign, over here.

00:12:23.573 --> 00:12:25.404
What is it?

00:12:25.442 --> 00:12:27.967
I detect traces of at least
five humanoid life-forms.

00:12:28.078 --> 00:12:29.545
Five?

00:12:29.579 --> 00:12:31.911
There were only three
on the away team.

00:12:31.948 --> 00:12:34.644
Evidently, they did not enter
this cavern alone.

00:13:00.543 --> 00:13:02.568
Are you in pain?

00:13:04.381 --> 00:13:06.975
It's... nothing.

00:13:08.718 --> 00:13:10.686
Remarkable.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.747
One of the symptoms
of the early stages of the phage

00:13:14.791 --> 00:13:17.954
is excruciating joint pain.

00:13:18.061 --> 00:13:21.963
I find it extraordinary
that you can endure it.

00:13:22.032 --> 00:13:24.057
Some who are infected

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:27.866
have been known to die
from the agony itself.

00:13:29.472 --> 00:13:34.034
It's going to take more
than an infection to kill me.

00:13:38.982 --> 00:13:41.576
It appears you are correct.

00:13:41.618 --> 00:13:46.112
Your body is successfully
fighting off the phage.

00:13:46.156 --> 00:13:48.190
I am overjoyed.

00:13:48.323 --> 00:13:50.985
How delightful for you.

00:13:51.092 --> 00:13:53.890
Soon we will begin
a series of procedures

00:13:53.929 --> 00:13:57.592
replicating your genetic code
and attempting various methods

00:13:57.632 --> 00:14:00.260
of integrating your DNA
with our own.

00:14:00.302 --> 00:14:03.237
In time, we'll be successful

00:14:03.271 --> 00:14:07.173
and eliminate the phage forever.

00:14:07.209 --> 00:14:09.939
When that time comes,

00:14:10.011 --> 00:14:13.276
you will be honored
as a hero by my people.

00:14:13.315 --> 00:14:17.411
I know I'm the first Klingon
you've ever seen,

00:14:17.452 --> 00:14:19.920
so I'll tell you

00:14:19.955 --> 00:14:26.758
that Klingons find honor
as warriors on the battlefield,

00:14:26.795 --> 00:14:31.425
not as guinea pigs
in a laboratory.

00:14:31.466 --> 00:14:35.425
Earlier, you accused me
of mutilating you.

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:38.871
Now you sound positively proud
to be Klingon.

00:14:41.076 --> 00:14:43.772
You have me to thank
for that, B'Elanna.

00:14:43.812 --> 00:14:45.973
You'll get no gratitude from me.

00:14:46.047 --> 00:14:49.881
Perhaps you'll feel
different in time.

00:14:49.918 --> 00:14:53.376
But I don't blame you
for your obstinance.

00:14:53.421 --> 00:14:55.218
I would be proud, too,

00:14:55.257 --> 00:14:58.158
with a form as handsome
as yours.

00:14:58.193 --> 00:15:01.458
I believe Klingons

00:15:01.496 --> 00:15:06.160
are the most impressive species
I have ever seen.

00:15:37.165 --> 00:15:38.689
Tom...

00:15:40.135 --> 00:15:41.102
Tom, wake up.

00:15:46.908 --> 00:15:48.808
B'Elanna?

00:15:48.843 --> 00:15:52.108
Yeah. It's me.

00:15:54.716 --> 00:15:57.082
B'Elanna, what have they
done to you?

00:16:08.463 --> 00:16:11.364
I remember them grabbing
us outside the caves

00:16:11.399 --> 00:16:13.367
and then I...

00:16:13.401 --> 00:16:15.733
I guess I just blacked out.

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:18.671
Yeah.
They stunned all of us.

00:16:18.707 --> 00:16:20.504
The next thing I knew,

00:16:20.542 --> 00:16:24.672
they were waking me up in
some kind of laboratory.

00:16:24.713 --> 00:16:28.615
I was so groggy I couldn't see.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:31.778
I asked them
what they had done to me

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:35.483
and then one of them said

00:16:35.523 --> 00:16:40.961
that they had completely
extracted my Klingon DNA.

00:16:42.597 --> 00:16:45.964
That doesn't seem possible...

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.434
but you look human.

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:53.203
I feel so weak
and sick to my stomach.

00:16:53.241 --> 00:16:54.970
Well, considering
what they've done to you,

00:16:55.043 --> 00:16:56.067
I'm not surprised.

00:17:02.484 --> 00:17:04.714
So strange.

00:17:04.753 --> 00:17:06.311
What?

00:17:06.354 --> 00:17:09.915
When I was a child,

00:17:10.024 --> 00:17:14.393
I did everything I could
to hide my forehead...

00:17:14.429 --> 00:17:17.489
hats, scarves... you name it.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:20.631
When I was a kid,

00:17:20.668 --> 00:17:22.158
I wore a cap
to cover the haircuts

00:17:22.203 --> 00:17:26.299
my father used to make me get,
first day of every summer.

00:17:31.346 --> 00:17:35.077
I grew up in a colony
on Kessik IV.

00:17:35.116 --> 00:17:37.414
My mother and I were
the only Klingons there,

00:17:37.452 --> 00:17:39.420
and that was a time

00:17:39.454 --> 00:17:42.617
when relations
between the Homeworld

00:17:42.657 --> 00:17:46.115
and the Federation
weren't too cordial.

00:17:46.161 --> 00:17:50.860
Nobody ever said anything,
but...

00:17:50.899 --> 00:17:53.663
we were different...

00:17:53.701 --> 00:17:55.669
and I didn't like that feeling.

00:17:58.072 --> 00:18:00.302
Then...

00:18:00.341 --> 00:18:03.902
my father left...

00:18:03.978 --> 00:18:06.776
when I was five years old.

00:18:08.316 --> 00:18:11.410
One day he was there,
and the next, he wasn't.

00:18:11.453 --> 00:18:15.287
I cried myself to sleep
every night

00:18:15.323 --> 00:18:17.416
for months...

00:18:17.459 --> 00:18:20.451
but of course,
I never told anybody.

00:18:22.697 --> 00:18:25.791
And then I finally decided

00:18:25.834 --> 00:18:29.895
that he left because
I looked like a Klingon...

00:18:32.474 --> 00:18:34.601
and so I tried to look human.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:42.147
Looks like you finally got
what you wanted.

00:19:03.171 --> 00:19:04.229
Strange.

00:19:04.272 --> 00:19:05.398
What is?

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:07.670
According to our last
geological scan,

00:19:07.709 --> 00:19:09.108
this cave should continue
straight ahead

00:19:09.143 --> 00:19:10.440
for another eight kilometers.

00:19:10.478 --> 00:19:13.072
This is solid granite,
more than 50 meters.

00:19:13.114 --> 00:19:15.014
If these caves were
changing configuration

00:19:15.049 --> 00:19:17.074
while we were here,
we certainly would've felt it.

00:19:17.118 --> 00:19:19.382
True, Commander,
but I do not believe

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.217
there has been
any tectonic activity.

00:19:21.256 --> 00:19:23.656
I believe this wall is
merely an illusion...

00:19:23.691 --> 00:19:26.922
a disguised force field.

00:19:26.961 --> 00:19:28.292
Away team to Voyager.

00:19:28.329 --> 00:19:29.557
Go ahead, Commander.

00:19:29.597 --> 00:19:32.088
We've run into some type
of force field, Captain.

00:19:32.133 --> 00:19:33.657
One minute, we were
reading an empty tunnel,

00:19:33.701 --> 00:19:34.861
and the next, we walked

00:19:34.903 --> 00:19:36.700
right into a solid wall of rock.

00:19:36.738 --> 00:19:38.672
Captain, the energy
configuration

00:19:38.706 --> 00:19:41.072
of the force field matrix
is virtually identical

00:19:41.109 --> 00:19:42.633
to those used by the Vidiians.

00:19:43.912 --> 00:19:45.402
Mr. Ayala...

00:19:45.446 --> 00:19:47.914
scan for any alien
vessels in the sector.

00:19:47.949 --> 00:19:49.678
Commander, we know
from past experience

00:19:49.717 --> 00:19:51.776
that our phasers
can disrupt that force field.

00:19:51.819 --> 00:19:53.377
I want to find out
what's in there.

00:19:53.421 --> 00:19:54.513
Aye, Captain.

00:19:54.556 --> 00:19:57.081
But I don't want you
taking any unnecessary risks.

00:19:57.125 --> 00:19:59.218
We'll be standing by to
implement an emergency beam-out.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:00.625
Acknowledged.

00:20:07.201 --> 00:20:08.532
It's not working, Captain.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:09.696
Try reconfiguring your phaser

00:20:09.737 --> 00:20:11.898
to match the bandwidth
modulation.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:12.929
Commander!

00:20:14.709 --> 00:20:15.801
Three to beam up!

00:20:37.765 --> 00:20:39.426
B'Elanna.

00:20:44.505 --> 00:20:48.134
How are you feeling today?

00:20:48.176 --> 00:20:50.974
I feel strong.

00:20:51.012 --> 00:20:55.108
It's very frustrating
to be restrained like this.

00:20:55.149 --> 00:20:56.616
I sympathize.

00:20:56.651 --> 00:21:01.145
I don't like being
chained up like an animal.

00:21:01.189 --> 00:21:03.089
I'm sorry.
I wish there was...

00:21:03.124 --> 00:21:05.786
I've been thinking about
what you've said.

00:21:05.827 --> 00:21:11.766
It's because of you
that I am Klingon.

00:21:11.799 --> 00:21:13.960
And I do...

00:21:14.035 --> 00:21:15.900
like...

00:21:15.937 --> 00:21:17.638
this feeling.

00:21:17.771 --> 00:21:20.296
In a strange way,

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:22.900
I suppose...

00:21:22.943 --> 00:21:24.740
I am grateful.

00:21:24.778 --> 00:21:26.746
Did you know

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:30.773
that Klingon females are
renowned in the Alpha Quadrant

00:21:30.817 --> 00:21:34.753
not only
for their physical prowess,

00:21:34.788 --> 00:21:36.756
but for their...

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:42.990
voracious...
sexual appetites as well?

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:47.194
Why not let your creation
out of her harness?

00:21:47.234 --> 00:21:51.466
Study her in action.

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:59.303
I wish it were possible,
B'Elanna...

00:22:00.981 --> 00:22:07.147
but I'm afraid I can't risk
releasing you just yet.

00:22:17.097 --> 00:22:18.428
Forgive me.

00:22:18.465 --> 00:22:19.796
For what?

00:22:19.833 --> 00:22:21.698
Please...

00:22:21.735 --> 00:22:24.465
don't condescend.

00:22:24.504 --> 00:22:28.497
I may have
a grotesque appearance,

00:22:28.542 --> 00:22:33.570
but I assure you
my instincts are finely honed,

00:22:33.613 --> 00:22:36.377
and I do have feelings.

00:22:40.921 --> 00:22:45.358
Hard as it may be
for you to imagine, B'Elanna,

00:22:45.392 --> 00:22:51.524
my people were once handsome
and vigorous like yours.

00:22:51.565 --> 00:22:56.628
And with your help,
we will be again.

00:22:56.670 --> 00:22:57.830
Perhaps, when that time comes...

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:04.641
I will not disgust you
quite so much as I do now.

00:23:16.723 --> 00:23:18.486
They're coming to take us
to the work detail.

00:23:18.525 --> 00:23:20.049
You can't let them see
how sick you are.

00:23:20.093 --> 00:23:21.424
Maybe if they
think I'm too weak,

00:23:21.461 --> 00:23:22.758
they'll leave me behind.

00:23:22.796 --> 00:23:24.957
I could try to get my hands
on that console over there.

00:23:25.065 --> 00:23:26.555
Or maybe they'll skip
the preliminaries

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:28.693
and take you straight
to organ processing.

00:23:35.876 --> 00:23:36.900
You.

00:23:36.943 --> 00:23:38.240
Come with me.

00:23:38.278 --> 00:23:39.438
What for?

00:23:39.479 --> 00:23:41.413
You asked to contact your ship.

00:23:41.448 --> 00:23:43.973
The Prefect wishes
to discuss your request.

00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:46.814
I'm the senior officer here.

00:23:46.853 --> 00:23:49.447
If your superiors want to talk
with one of us, it should be me.

00:23:50.557 --> 00:23:52.457
He's not going
anywhere without me!

00:23:52.492 --> 00:23:53.459
Tom, don't.

00:23:53.493 --> 00:23:54.653
They'll kill you.

00:23:54.694 --> 00:23:55.683
Stop!

00:23:56.663 --> 00:23:59.564
It's okay, Tom.

00:23:59.599 --> 00:24:01.726
They're the ones
with the guns, remember?

00:24:16.950 --> 00:24:19.043
What is it?

00:24:25.992 --> 00:24:27.687
Now that the Vidiians
know we're here,

00:24:27.727 --> 00:24:29.319
we have to be prepared
for the possibility

00:24:29.362 --> 00:24:31.694
that they'll call in
reinforcements.

00:24:31.731 --> 00:24:32.857
So far, long-range sensors

00:24:32.899 --> 00:24:34.958
haven't located
any alien vessels near here.

00:24:35.035 --> 00:24:37.299
However, it is possible
that the same technology

00:24:37.337 --> 00:24:38.531
that disguises
their force fields,

00:24:38.572 --> 00:24:39.971
cloaks their ships.

00:24:40.073 --> 00:24:41.973
The other thing
we have to consider

00:24:42.075 --> 00:24:44.270
is that the prisoners
may be at greater risk now.

00:24:44.311 --> 00:24:46.836
Captain, take a look at this.

00:24:46.880 --> 00:24:48.211
Using our tricorder data,

00:24:48.248 --> 00:24:49.647
I've been able
to scan the entire planet

00:24:49.683 --> 00:24:50.980
for the force field signature,

00:24:51.017 --> 00:24:52.541
and it looks like
the field surrounds an area

00:24:52.586 --> 00:24:54.349
more than 600 kilometers
in circumference.

00:24:54.387 --> 00:24:56.480
Is there any way
to scan inside it?

00:24:56.523 --> 00:24:59.424
Every reconfiguration
I've tried has failed.

00:24:59.459 --> 00:25:01.086
If it's the same kind
of force field

00:25:01.127 --> 00:25:03.357
the Vidiians used
the last time we ran into them,

00:25:03.396 --> 00:25:05.421
why didn't our phasers
breach it?

00:25:05.465 --> 00:25:08.628
Apparently, it has been adapted
to repulse phaser fire.

00:25:08.668 --> 00:25:11.660
If the Vidiians can move in
and out of there, so can we.

00:25:11.705 --> 00:25:13.229
Start setting up simulations.

00:25:13.273 --> 00:25:15.468
Find a way to get through
that force field.

00:25:22.082 --> 00:25:24.209
B'Elanna?

00:25:26.786 --> 00:25:30.017
I have something
I want to show you.

00:25:37.998 --> 00:25:39.966
Durst...

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:41.433
I thought perhaps this new face

00:25:41.468 --> 00:25:43.766
would make you
more comfortable with me.

00:25:43.803 --> 00:25:46.169
You've killed him.

00:25:46.206 --> 00:25:47.503
Yes, B'Elanna,

00:25:47.540 --> 00:25:51.237
but his organs will save
more than a dozen lives.

00:26:14.100 --> 00:26:16.364
Deep-level scans have revealed
a network of microfissures,

00:26:16.403 --> 00:26:17.836
minuscule openings
which develop briefly

00:26:17.871 --> 00:26:20.339
each time the field
matrix remodulates.

00:26:20.373 --> 00:26:22.534
Just how small are
these microfissures?

00:26:22.575 --> 00:26:24.770
Less than one micron.

00:26:24.811 --> 00:26:26.904
And they close up
within a few seconds.

00:26:26.947 --> 00:26:28.915
Would it be possible
to use our phasers

00:26:28.949 --> 00:26:31.281
to expand one of these
openings as it's forming?

00:26:31.318 --> 00:26:32.910
That was our first thought.

00:26:32.953 --> 00:26:35.615
But we realized such an attempt
would have to be at close range

00:26:35.655 --> 00:26:36.883
and would carry the risk

00:26:36.923 --> 00:26:39.289
of alerting the Vidiians
to our presence.

00:26:39.326 --> 00:26:40.520
So then it occurred to us...

00:26:40.560 --> 00:26:42.221
if we could narrow
the transporter's energy beam

00:26:42.262 --> 00:26:44.196
tightly enough,
it might be possible

00:26:44.230 --> 00:26:47.222
to transport one of us
through the microfissures.

00:26:47.267 --> 00:26:48.962
Of course, timing the transport

00:26:49.069 --> 00:26:51.799
to the precise moment
of an opening would be critical.

00:26:51.838 --> 00:26:53.931
But if we could
get someone inside,

00:26:53.974 --> 00:26:55.601
we might be able
to find our people

00:26:55.642 --> 00:26:58.076
and also deactivate
the force field.

00:26:58.111 --> 00:26:59.339
And then, presumably,

00:26:59.379 --> 00:27:01.210
we could beam everyone
back to the ship.

00:27:01.247 --> 00:27:02.544
Precisely.

00:27:02.582 --> 00:27:04.914
But you should be aware
that because we are incapable

00:27:05.018 --> 00:27:06.485
of scanning beyond
the force field,

00:27:06.519 --> 00:27:08.180
we will have no way
of communicating

00:27:08.221 --> 00:27:10.155
with whoever
transports inside it,

00:27:10.190 --> 00:27:11.487
nor will we be able to verify

00:27:11.524 --> 00:27:13.719
that the transport
has been successfully completed.

00:27:13.760 --> 00:27:17.127
Moreover, what's to prevent
whoever goes in

00:27:17.163 --> 00:27:19.393
from being captured
by the Vidiians?

00:27:19.432 --> 00:27:21.957
I have an idea about that,
Captain.

00:27:23.436 --> 00:27:25.267
Dermal stimulator, please.

00:27:29.776 --> 00:27:31.767
Remarkable work, Doctor.

00:27:32.946 --> 00:27:34.208
If you think this is remarkable,

00:27:34.247 --> 00:27:35.942
you should see me
remove a bunion.

00:27:40.820 --> 00:27:43.618
I have done my best
to replicate Vidiian attire.

00:27:43.656 --> 00:27:46.284
I trust it will prove
sufficiently convincing.

00:27:47.727 --> 00:27:50.457
It's a fine piece
of work, Mr. Tuvok.

00:27:50.497 --> 00:27:53.666
Next time I need a tailor,
I'll know just where to look.

00:27:54.667 --> 00:27:55.964
Quickly now!

00:28:00.773 --> 00:28:02.263
In there!

00:28:20.192 --> 00:28:22.353
Here, B'Elanna.

00:28:22.394 --> 00:28:23.520
Sit down.

00:28:29.234 --> 00:28:32.032
Here. It's water.

00:28:33.572 --> 00:28:34.630
Thanks.

00:28:36.775 --> 00:28:38.072
Rest while you can.

00:28:38.110 --> 00:28:39.907
The guard won't be back
right away.

00:28:41.780 --> 00:28:43.645
Keep it.

00:28:51.523 --> 00:28:53.889
Tom...

00:28:53.926 --> 00:28:55.291
I've been thinking.

00:28:57.763 --> 00:29:00.789
When they did this thing to me,

00:29:00.833 --> 00:29:03.597
I think it changed more
than just the way I look.

00:29:03.635 --> 00:29:05.398
What do you mean?

00:29:08.941 --> 00:29:12.843
Back there,
when they took Durst away...

00:29:12.878 --> 00:29:15.039
I was...

00:29:15.080 --> 00:29:16.638
terrified.

00:29:16.682 --> 00:29:19.515
No one could blame you for that.

00:29:19.551 --> 00:29:22.019
You don't understand.

00:29:22.054 --> 00:29:24.045
I've been in worse situations,

00:29:24.089 --> 00:29:26.853
but I've never felt
like that before.

00:29:26.892 --> 00:29:28.416
Never.

00:29:28.460 --> 00:29:29.825
I mean...

00:29:29.862 --> 00:29:34.356
my heart was pounding
and my hands were shaking.

00:29:34.399 --> 00:29:36.890
I didn't even try to help you.

00:29:36.935 --> 00:29:38.300
B'Elanna, I'm no doctor,

00:29:38.337 --> 00:29:40.805
but I have to believe
that whatever they did to you

00:29:40.839 --> 00:29:42.807
has seriously depleted
your strength.

00:29:42.841 --> 00:29:44.468
There's nothing
you could've done.

00:29:44.510 --> 00:29:47.206
No, that's not it.

00:29:47.246 --> 00:29:49.441
I think that...

00:29:49.481 --> 00:29:52.939
when they extracted
my Klingon DNA...

00:29:53.051 --> 00:29:55.349
they turned me
into some kind of...

00:29:57.556 --> 00:29:58.921
...a coward.

00:30:00.092 --> 00:30:03.550
Sometimes fear
can be a good thing.

00:30:03.595 --> 00:30:07.190
It keeps you from taking
unnecessary chances.

00:30:07.232 --> 00:30:10.668
Courage doesn't mean
that you don't have fear.

00:30:10.702 --> 00:30:13.364
It means that you've
learned to overcome it.

00:30:13.405 --> 00:30:16.465
And I know you can find
the courage to hold on

00:30:16.508 --> 00:30:19.375
until we can find a way
out of this place.

00:30:19.411 --> 00:30:21.709
What's going on here?

00:30:21.747 --> 00:30:23.715
She's ill.
She needed a rest.

00:30:23.749 --> 00:30:25.444
If she's too weak, I'll take
her back to the barracks.

00:30:25.484 --> 00:30:26.508
That's okay, Tom.

00:30:26.552 --> 00:30:28.213
Maybe from there,

00:30:28.253 --> 00:30:29.811
I can try to make contact
with the ship.

00:30:38.096 --> 00:30:40.496
The emitter array has been
initialized, Captain.

00:30:40.532 --> 00:30:41.499
Good.

00:30:41.533 --> 00:30:43.194
Are you ready, Mr. Chakotay?

00:30:45.771 --> 00:30:48.365
Captain, there's an opening
forming in the force field.

00:30:48.407 --> 00:30:49.772
Initiating auto sequence.

00:30:49.808 --> 00:30:51.469
Targeting scanners
to match coordinates.

00:30:51.510 --> 00:30:52.977
Scanners locked.

00:30:53.011 --> 00:30:54.740
On my mark, Mr. Kim.

00:30:56.782 --> 00:30:58.147
Energize.

00:31:03.789 --> 00:31:05.256
Well...

00:31:05.290 --> 00:31:06.723
now we wait.

00:31:17.970 --> 00:31:20.495
Make a sound
and I'll break your neck.

00:31:20.539 --> 00:31:22.336
Understand?

00:31:22.374 --> 00:31:25.741
I'm looking for my friend,
Tom Paris... a human male.

00:31:25.777 --> 00:31:26.766
Have you seen him?

00:31:26.812 --> 00:31:27.972
He was here,

00:31:28.046 --> 00:31:29.536
but they sent him
to another tunnel.

00:31:29.581 --> 00:31:30.741
Which one?

00:31:30.782 --> 00:31:32.579
Back that way.

00:31:32.618 --> 00:31:34.085
There was another human
with him,

00:31:34.119 --> 00:31:36.986
but they took her
back to the barracks.

00:31:37.022 --> 00:31:38.580
A human female?

00:31:38.624 --> 00:31:39.886
Yeah...

00:31:52.070 --> 00:31:54.061
I need your help here.

00:32:40.719 --> 00:32:42.186
What are you doing?!

00:32:42.220 --> 00:32:44.188
Come with us.

00:32:44.222 --> 00:32:45.246
Where are you taking me?

00:32:45.290 --> 00:32:46.689
For a shower and a hot meal.

00:32:46.725 --> 00:32:48.090
No, please!

00:34:08.240 --> 00:34:09.468
Wake up, pahtk!

00:34:10.475 --> 00:34:11.908
Eat!

00:34:11.943 --> 00:34:15.242
What... what is it?

00:34:15.280 --> 00:34:17.305
Some rodent I killed.

00:34:19.951 --> 00:34:21.942
No. Thanks.

00:34:22.020 --> 00:34:25.285
I'm sorry I can't
replicate you a soufflé,

00:34:25.323 --> 00:34:27.154
but you need nourishment.

00:34:27.192 --> 00:34:29.820
I can't carry you
all the way out of here.

00:34:40.038 --> 00:34:42.939
How are we supposed
to escape this place?

00:34:42.974 --> 00:34:44.703
There are guards everywhere.

00:34:44.743 --> 00:34:46.335
We fight our way out.

00:34:46.378 --> 00:34:47.743
Maybe you haven't noticed,

00:34:47.779 --> 00:34:50.680
but I'm not exactly
in fighting form.

00:34:50.715 --> 00:34:53.284
That's why you need food.
Eat!

00:34:59.523 --> 00:35:01.252
So...

00:35:01.292 --> 00:35:02.657
you're what's left over

00:35:02.693 --> 00:35:05.457
when all the Klingon DNA
is taken out.

00:35:09.366 --> 00:35:11.095
Apparently.

00:35:11.135 --> 00:35:13.126
If I hadn't come along,

00:35:13.170 --> 00:35:16.037
were you just going to waste
away in that prison camp

00:35:16.073 --> 00:35:18.541
until they killed you
for your body parts?

00:35:18.575 --> 00:35:21.635
Were you too frightened to act?

00:35:21.679 --> 00:35:24.546
I was looking
for a way to escape.

00:35:24.581 --> 00:35:25.548
Looking!

00:35:25.582 --> 00:35:27.675
I'll show you the way to escape.

00:35:27.718 --> 00:35:30.050
This and this.

00:35:30.087 --> 00:35:32.681
That's the way you respond
to every situation, isn't it?

00:35:32.723 --> 00:35:34.315
If it doesn't work, hit it.

00:35:34.358 --> 00:35:36.588
If it's in your way,
knock it down.

00:35:37.961 --> 00:35:40.225
No wonder
I got kicked out of the Academy.

00:35:40.264 --> 00:35:44.098
For which you should be
eternally grateful.

00:35:44.134 --> 00:35:45.431
Well, I'm not.

00:35:45.469 --> 00:35:47.733
Your temper has gotten me into
trouble more times than I can...

00:35:50.174 --> 00:35:51.539
Listen to me.

00:35:57.514 --> 00:36:00.847
Listen to us.

00:36:00.884 --> 00:36:02.545
This is ridiculous.

00:36:02.586 --> 00:36:06.181
Do you realize that we're each
fighting with our self?

00:36:06.223 --> 00:36:09.056
I'm not the one
who's fighting, pahtk.

00:36:09.093 --> 00:36:10.754
If I remember correctly,

00:36:10.794 --> 00:36:13.888
I'm the one who rescued you
from that prison

00:36:13.931 --> 00:36:16.092
and carried you here.

00:36:16.133 --> 00:36:18.101
Don't you think

00:36:18.135 --> 00:36:21.468
you could at least
acknowledge that?

00:36:21.505 --> 00:36:23.939
Can't you even admit

00:36:24.041 --> 00:36:26.373
that you won't be able
to get out of here without me?

00:36:27.544 --> 00:36:30.479
I don't know that I can
get out of here with you.

00:36:30.514 --> 00:36:31.947
Brute force
isn't going to do it.

00:36:32.015 --> 00:36:36.145
Maybe not!
Maybe we'll die in the attempt,

00:36:36.186 --> 00:36:37.813
but that's better
than sitting here

00:36:37.855 --> 00:36:39.914
like frightened Tika cats
doing nothing!

00:36:39.957 --> 00:36:42.824
There you go again...
out of control.

00:36:42.860 --> 00:36:44.953
Just leaping into action

00:36:45.062 --> 00:36:46.654
before you think things through.

00:36:46.697 --> 00:36:48.221
Fine! You stay here.
I'm getting out.

00:36:48.265 --> 00:36:49.232
No, wait a minute.

00:36:49.266 --> 00:36:50.233
That's not what I meant.

00:36:50.267 --> 00:36:51.256
I'm sorry.

00:36:52.569 --> 00:36:53.900
Please...

00:36:58.642 --> 00:37:01.110
Just before...

00:37:01.145 --> 00:37:02.476
you rescued me...

00:37:05.149 --> 00:37:07.811
I logged onto the
Vidiians' computer system.

00:37:07.851 --> 00:37:09.148
I only had a few seconds,

00:37:09.186 --> 00:37:12.519
but I think I found a way
to access the force field

00:37:12.556 --> 00:37:15.684
that's cloaking this place.

00:37:15.726 --> 00:37:18.559
With a few minutes more,
I could've deactivated it.

00:37:18.595 --> 00:37:21.120
Then Voyager
could get a lock on us.

00:37:21.165 --> 00:37:22.393
Beam us back.

00:37:22.433 --> 00:37:24.128
Paris, too.

00:37:24.168 --> 00:37:26.864
It may not be as exciting

00:37:26.904 --> 00:37:29.464
as fighting our way out,

00:37:29.506 --> 00:37:32.532
but it stands a much
better chance of working

00:37:32.576 --> 00:37:36.535
if... I have your help.

00:37:38.682 --> 00:37:42.140
So... you need me.

00:37:45.022 --> 00:37:48.480
I can't get back
to that computer without you

00:37:48.525 --> 00:37:51.016
and you'll have to cover
for me while I work.

00:37:53.464 --> 00:37:55.659
We can't go
to the prison barracks.

00:37:55.699 --> 00:37:58.167
There are
too many guards there.

00:37:58.202 --> 00:38:00.170
In the lab,
where they were holding me,

00:38:00.204 --> 00:38:02.468
there was a security console.

00:38:02.506 --> 00:38:05.168
That's the last place
they would expect us to be.

00:38:20.390 --> 00:38:23.689
They must have taken her
to organ processing.

00:38:23.727 --> 00:38:25.661
Tell me how to get there.

00:38:27.331 --> 00:38:28.662
Keep your hands off me!

00:38:28.699 --> 00:38:30.189
Whatever you say, Paris,

00:38:30.234 --> 00:38:32.600
but I thought you might like
to get out of this place.

00:38:35.239 --> 00:38:36.866
Chakotay?

00:38:36.907 --> 00:38:38.807
Where are Torres and Durst?

00:38:41.812 --> 00:38:42.870
I think they've been taken

00:38:42.913 --> 00:38:44.881
to what the Vidiians
call "organ processing."

00:38:44.915 --> 00:38:46.143
You!

00:38:46.183 --> 00:38:47.411
Why are you talking
to that prisoner?

00:38:47.451 --> 00:38:49.817
I was ordered to take him
to organ processing.

00:38:49.853 --> 00:38:51.650
Why wasn't I notified?

00:38:51.688 --> 00:38:53.019
I was told you had been.

00:38:54.391 --> 00:38:56.291
I've never seen you before.

00:38:56.326 --> 00:38:59.853
My face was just grafted.

00:39:03.534 --> 00:39:05.001
Very well.

00:39:05.035 --> 00:39:06.696
Take him, but from now on,

00:39:06.737 --> 00:39:10.229
I expect to be notified in
advance of all transfers.

00:39:10.274 --> 00:39:11.502
Yes, sir.

00:39:20.884 --> 00:39:22.511
There.

00:39:23.720 --> 00:39:26.086
I have to bypass
the security code,

00:39:26.123 --> 00:39:28.489
so I can access
the force field grid.

00:39:28.525 --> 00:39:33.462
Then I'll have a better idea
of what we're dealing with.

00:39:34.932 --> 00:39:36.923
That should do it.

00:39:38.135 --> 00:39:39.261
There.

00:39:39.303 --> 00:39:40.930
That's what we're up against,

00:39:41.038 --> 00:39:42.232
and I think we're...

00:39:42.272 --> 00:39:43.739
here.

00:39:43.774 --> 00:39:44.934
Can you shut it down?

00:39:45.042 --> 00:39:46.441
I'm working on it.

00:39:47.744 --> 00:39:49.302
What now?

00:39:50.314 --> 00:39:51.303
If they didn't know

00:39:51.348 --> 00:39:52.815
we were here before,
they do now.

00:39:55.819 --> 00:39:57.548
Take it easy.

00:39:57.588 --> 00:39:58.850
I'll be done in a minute.

00:40:01.625 --> 00:40:05.186
You're not frightened
anymore, are you?

00:40:05.228 --> 00:40:07.219
Maybe I just don't have time
to think about it.

00:40:12.002 --> 00:40:12.934
Are you hurt?

00:40:12.970 --> 00:40:14.267
Keep working!

00:40:14.304 --> 00:40:15.430
B'Elanna!

00:40:15.472 --> 00:40:16.700
Stop.

00:40:16.740 --> 00:40:19.504
You're not going to hurt me.

00:40:19.543 --> 00:40:21.170
You need me.

00:40:21.211 --> 00:40:25.978
You're right,
but if you do not surrender,

00:40:26.049 --> 00:40:27.983
I will kill her.

00:40:28.085 --> 00:40:29.814
Drop it!

00:40:35.192 --> 00:40:36.887
Who are you?

00:40:36.927 --> 00:40:38.121
That's what I want to know!

00:40:38.161 --> 00:40:39.492
It's Chakotay.

00:40:42.966 --> 00:40:45.560
I think I've just about accessed
the force field.

00:40:45.602 --> 00:40:46.967
Hurry!

00:40:49.306 --> 00:40:50.796
Got it!

00:40:50.841 --> 00:40:52.331
There.

00:40:53.777 --> 00:40:56.075
Captain, the force field
has been disrupted.

00:40:57.214 --> 00:41:00.115
Mr. Kim, can you get a lock
on Commander Chakotay?

00:41:00.150 --> 00:41:01.276
Chakotay to Voyager.
Do you read?

00:41:01.318 --> 00:41:03.343
Loud and clear, Commander.

00:41:03.387 --> 00:41:04.649
I found them, Captain.

00:41:05.956 --> 00:41:07.890
No!

00:41:09.860 --> 00:41:11.191
No!

00:41:11.228 --> 00:41:15.255
Three humans and one Klingon
to beam up.

00:41:24.608 --> 00:41:27.304
She's badly wounded, Captain.

00:41:27.344 --> 00:41:28.311
Beam her to Sick Bay!

00:41:28.345 --> 00:41:31.212
Don't. No time.

00:41:36.687 --> 00:41:39.622
You showed true courage.

00:41:39.656 --> 00:41:45.754
It makes my death...
an honorable one.

00:42:07.216 --> 00:42:08.911
Using tissue
from your counterpart,

00:42:08.951 --> 00:42:11.545
I can replicate the Klingon DNA.

00:42:11.587 --> 00:42:13.054
Then, over the course
of several days,

00:42:13.088 --> 00:42:14.749
I'll reintegrate
that genetic material

00:42:14.790 --> 00:42:16.223
into your cellular structure.

00:42:16.258 --> 00:42:17.953
Wait a minute...
you're not saying

00:42:18.026 --> 00:42:19.459
that you're going
to change me back.

00:42:19.494 --> 00:42:21.189
That's precisely
what I'm saying.

00:42:22.431 --> 00:42:24.092
Your cells' ability
to synthesize proteins

00:42:24.132 --> 00:42:26.692
has been severely compromised.

00:42:26.735 --> 00:42:28.669
You need the Klingon
genes to survive.

00:42:32.874 --> 00:42:36.674
So, she's saving my life again.

00:42:36.712 --> 00:42:38.202
I'll get started on the DNA.

00:42:45.921 --> 00:42:48.355
How are you doing?

00:42:48.390 --> 00:42:51.359
I'm not sure.

00:42:51.393 --> 00:42:53.554
It's been a pretty
strange experience.

00:42:53.595 --> 00:42:58.692
I do know that right now...

00:42:58.734 --> 00:43:02.830
the way I am...

00:43:02.871 --> 00:43:06.432
I'm more at peace with myself
than I've ever been before...

00:43:09.111 --> 00:43:11.705
...and that's a good feeling.

00:43:11.747 --> 00:43:14.307
But?

00:43:14.349 --> 00:43:17.750
I'm incomplete.

00:43:19.688 --> 00:43:23.556
It doesn't feel like me.

00:43:27.763 --> 00:43:30.630
I guess I've had someone else
living inside of me for too long

00:43:30.666 --> 00:43:32.657
to feel right without her.

00:43:32.701 --> 00:43:35.670
I'd have to say that you two
made quite a team down there.

00:43:38.140 --> 00:43:41.803
I know.

00:43:41.843 --> 00:43:46.542
I came to admire
a lot of things about her...

00:43:46.581 --> 00:43:49.448
her strength,

00:43:49.484 --> 00:43:51.475
her bravery...

00:43:58.827 --> 00:44:03.230
I guess... I just have
to accept the fact

00:44:03.265 --> 00:44:06.063
that I'll spend the rest
of my life fighting with her.
